From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:59:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nslcd: fix the abort on shutdown

Stopping nslcd always ended with SIGABRT ("*** bit out of range 0 -
FD_SETSIZE on fd_set ***: terminated"): the main thread set
nslcd_serversocket to -1 after closing it while worker threads were still
in their accept loop, and the next FD_SET() in a worker hit the
_FORTIFY_SOURCE check.

Backport of the two shutdown fixes released in nss-pam-ldapd 0.9.13:

  b7841fc5647fafcea9258e13190ee2058dd4e7b0
  "Do not pass invalid file descriptor to FD_ISSET()"
  https://github.com/arthurdejong/nss-pam-ldapd/commit/b7841fc5647fafcea9258e13190ee2058dd4e7b0
  (byte-identical apart from line offsets)

  ed4041ca4cd8a7642340b791f3782d2df52c1a8e
  "Do not try to kill thread that was successfully joined"
  https://github.com/arthurdejong/nss-pam-ldapd/commit/ed4041ca4cd8a7642340b791f3782d2df52c1a8e
  (adapted)

Upstream's second commit tests pthread_timedjoin_np() == -1 and errno
against EBUSY, but the function returns an error number, never -1, and
does not set errno, so its "still running" message never fires. Here the
result is checked directly; ETIMEDOUT is the value it returns when the
thread is still running after the existing 3 s shutdown deadline.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 nslcd/nslcd.c | 21 +++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nslcd/nslcd.c b/nslcd/nslcd.c
--- a/nslcd/nslcd.c
+++ b/nslcd/nslcd.c
@@ -200,13 +200,6 @@ static void sig_handler(int signum)
 /* do some cleaning up before terminating */
 static void exithandler(void)
 {
-  /* close socket if it's still in use */
-  if (nslcd_serversocket >= 0)
-  {
-    if (close(nslcd_serversocket))
-      log_log(LOG_WARNING, "problem closing server socket (ignored): %s",
-              strerror(errno));
-  }
   /* remove existing named socket */
   if (unlink(NSLCD_SOCKET) < 0)
   {
@@ -687,6 +680,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
   sigset_t signalmask, oldmask;
 #ifdef HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP
   struct timespec ts;
+  int rc;
 #endif /* HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP */
   /* block all these signals so our worker threads won't handle them */
   sigemptyset(&signalmask);
@@ -891,7 +885,6 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
               i, strerror(errno));
   /* close server socket to trigger failures in threads waiting on accept() */
   close(nslcd_serversocket);
-  nslcd_serversocket = -1;
   /* if we can, wait a few seconds for the threads to finish */
 #ifdef HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP
   ts.tv_sec = time(NULL) + 3;
@@ -900,10 +893,18 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
   for (i = 0; i < nslcd_cfg->threads; i++)
   {
 #ifdef HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP
-    pthread_timedjoin_np(nslcd_threads[i], NULL, &ts);
-#endif /* HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP */
+    rc = pthread_timedjoin_np(nslcd_threads[i], NULL, &ts);
+    if (rc != 0)
+    {
+      if (rc != ETIMEDOUT)
+        log_log(LOG_ERR, "thread %d cannot be joined (ignoring): %s",
+                i, strerror(rc));
+      log_log(LOG_ERR, "thread %d is still running, shutting down anyway", i);
+    }
+#else
     if (pthread_kill(nslcd_threads[i], 0) == 0)
       log_log(LOG_ERR, "thread %d is still running, shutting down anyway", i);
+#endif /* HAVE_PTHREAD_TIMEDJOIN_NP */
   }
   /* we're done */
   return EXIT_SUCCESS;
-- 
2.53.0

